sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2019-boundary-03> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2019-boundary-03--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2019-boundary-03--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on levin-2019-boundary-03: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.47" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.469"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "partially-resolvable" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.58"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "A set point is operationalized here as restoration of organ geometry after perturbation, which is a real measurement. The cited Xenopus, salamander, and tubule results were published as measurements and can be compiled for a subset of the scope. They are not one downloadable morphometric table, and a local developmental program predicts the same restorations. Existing literature can pressure the claim on those examples and cannot settle the cognitive wording or the full vertebrate scope." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: After a defined perturbation (scrambled craniofacial primordia, a tail graft, or an enlarged tubule cell), measure whether the collective returns to the species-typical organ geometry rather than to a locally stable wrong shape. Return to the target supports a large-scale set point; stable wrong anatomies after the same perturbations would refute it." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "The classic cases are spread across papers and taxa, with no shared landmark file.", "Return to normal shape is also predicted by local gene-regulatory programs.", "Kidney-tubule and salamander graft results are not in Xenbase." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2019-boundary-03--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of levin-2019-boundary-03 by Grok 4.7: 0.72" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-operationalizability> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0/operationalizability" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.72"^^xsd:double ;
